thricken for OS-9/68000=======================ORIG holds comp.sources.games volume 13, issue 101 (thricken, one part) withissue 102's Patch1 as `patches01'.  The files beside it are the post withPatch1 applied and the OS-9 changes below; the data files are inGAMES/THRICKEN.The game is ANSI C throughout, which Microware's K&R `cc' will not read.`ansi2knr' could not do the work here: it converts a definition only when thefunction NAME is at the left margin, and every one of thricken's 16definitions writes the return type on the same line, so it converted none ofthem -- and it never touches declarations.  All 16 definitions and all 16declarations were converted by hand.What changed, and why:  thricken.h   The globals are defined in the header, which every file               includes; l68 takes the second definition as a clash, so each               is TGLOBAL -- extern everywhere but main.c, which defines them.               LIBDIR, the data directory the Makefile passes as a -D, is               /dd/GAMES/THRICKEN here.               curses' cbreak() only sets a flag on this system; it does not               put the terminal in character mode, so stdio's getchar() still               waits for a whole line.  getch() is the read that honours it,               and that is what getchar() is under OSK.               strdup() is not declared by this C library and every use of its               result was read as an int.  main.c       `q' left the game with kill(getpid(),SIGINT); there is no               kill() here, so it calls cleanup(), which is what that signal               would have run.               ^C interrupts the key read and unix.l runs the handler only at               check_signal(), so the key loop calls it.  screen.c     SIGTSTP does not exist here, so the job-control handler is not               installed and stop() has nothing to do.  myerror() slept with               sleep(); this C library has tsleep(), which counts ticks.files.c, scores.c, extern.h and patchlevel.h differ from the post only in theK&R conversion.  getpwuid() comes from the build driver's own shim, whichanswers with $USER.Measured under os9exec: the first screen, `Cyclic Madness', draws with itssprite map and status panel; h, j, k and l move the player and the panelcounts the moves; ^C leaves the game.  The high score file isGAMES/THRICKEN/scores and ships empty, as the post's does.Build: cc files.c main.c scores.c screen.c ../unixlib/strdup.c          ../unixlib/getopt.c -DOSK -l=curses.l -l=termlib.l